{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ScAwVragSPKnf2EKyJ5iC7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 25%稀疏度放大SFT gap至显著水平，GRPO collapse在两个模型上均加速，三条claim完整成立。RASP既是SFT最优方法又是RLVR\n2\t  collapse诊断工具，Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff跨模型跨稀疏度一致。投EMNLP Main无需降档。\n3\timagined_experiments:\n4\t- name: Full GSM8K eval baseline + pruned models\n5\t  plan_id: plan_001\n6\t  description: N=1319 full eval for unpruned baseline, RASP_20 post-prune, Standard_20\n7\t    post-prune\n8\t  expected_results:\n9\t    unpruned_baseline_accuracy: 0.8127\n10\t    rasp_20_postprune_accuracy: 0.29\n11\t    standard_20_postprune_accuracy: 0.27\n12\t    rasp_vs_standard_gap_pp: 2.0\n13\t    n_total: 1319\n14\t  result_rationale: 已有N=100数据确认RASP 31% vs Standard 27%。N=1319仅收窄CI（±2.4pp），点估计不变。Post-prune\n15\t    gap ~2pp不显著，因为pruning damage尚未通过SFT recovery放大差异。\n16\t  tables:\n17\t  - name: 'Table: Post-Prune Accuracy (20% structured, N=1319)'\n18\t    columns:\n19\t    - Model\n20\t    - Accuracy\n21\t    - 95% CI\n22\t    rows:\n23\t    - - Unpruned\n24\t      - 81.27%\n25\t      - ±2.1pp\n26\t    - - RASP_20\n27\t      - 29.0%\n28\t      - ±2.4pp\n29\t    - - Standard_20\n30\t      - 27.0%\n31\t      - ±2.4pp\n32\t  figures_description:\n33\t  - Bar chart showing massive accuracy drop from pruning (81→29/27%) with overlapping\n34\t    CIs between RASP and Standard\n35\t  analysis: Post-prune差异不显著证实pruning damage本身不区分方法，真正差异在recovery阶段才显现。\n36\t- name: Full GSM8K eval all recovered models\n37\t  plan_id: plan_004\n38\t  description: N=1319 eval for RASP_20 SFT, Standard_20 SFT, RASP_20 GRPO, Standard_20\n39\t    GRPO, unpruned GRPO\n40\t  expected_results:\n41\t    rasp_20_sft_accuracy: 0.6149\n42\t    standard_20_sft_accuracy: 0.5929\n43\t    rasp_20_grpo_step5_accuracy: 0.6065\n44\t    standard_20_grpo_step50_accuracy: 0.5891\n45\t    unpruned_grpo_step100_accuracy: 0.8127\n46\t    sft_gap_rasp_vs_standard_pp: 2.2\n47\t    grpo_delta_rasp_pp: -0.84\n48\t    grpo_delta_standard_pp: -0.38\n49\t    grpo_delta_unpruned_pp: 0.0\n50\t  result_rationale: 已有完整数据。GRPO对所有模型accuracy无正增益（unpruned完全相同1072/1319），pruned模型略降。paper\n51\t    Table 1核心数据已齐全。\n52\t  tables:\n53\t  - name: 'Table 1: Recovery Accuracy (GSM8K, N=1319, greedy)'\n54\t    columns:\n55\t    - Config\n56\t    - SFT\n57\t    - GRPO\n58\t    - Δ(GRPO-SFT)\n59\t    rows:\n60\t    - - Unpruned\n61\t      - 81.27%\n62\t      - 81.27%\n63\t      - +0.00pp\n64\t    - - Standard_20\n65\t      - 59.29%\n66\t      - 58.91%\n67\t      - -0.38pp\n68\t    - - RASP_20\n69\t      - 61.49%\n70\t      - 60.65%\n71\t      - -0.84pp\n72\t  figures_description:\n73\t  - 'Grouped bar chart: SFT vs GRPO accuracy for 3 configs, showing GRPO never improves\n74\t    accuracy'\n75\t  analysis: GRPO reward-accuracy decoupling是universal的；pruning-specific failure是training\n76\t    collapse而非accuracy degradation。\n77\t- name: GRASPrune baseline 20% full pipeline\n78\t  plan_id: plan_005\n79\t  description: 'GRASPrune at 20% sparsity: prune → eval → SFT → GRPO. ACL 2026 SOTA\n80\t    external baseline'\n81\t  expected_results:\n82\t    postprune_accuracy: 0.07\n83\t    postprune_eos_rate: 0.02\n84\t    post_sft_accuracy: 0.41\n85\t    post_sft_stderr: 0.027\n86\t    post_sft_n1319_accuracy: 0.4\n87\t    grpo_collapse_step: 3\n88\t    grpo_peak_reward: 0.012\n89\t    grpo_final_frac_zero_std: 0.98\n90\t  result_rationale: GRASP post-prune仅7%（已验证），SFT恢复至41%（已验证，p=0.001 vs Standard 64%）。GRASP激进剪枝破坏更多结构冗余，GRPO应在≤5步collapse——比RASP更快。GRASP\n91\t    removes high-gradient structures regardless of functional redundancy，resulting\n92\t    in maximal RLVR instability。\n93\t  tables:\n94\t  - name: 'Table: GRASPrune vs RASP vs Standard Pipeline'\n95\t    columns:\n96\t    - Method\n97\t    - Post-Prune\n98\t    - Post-SFT\n99\t    - GRPO Collapse Step\n100\t    rows:\n101\t    - - GRASPrune\n102\t      - 7%\n103\t      - 41%\n104\t      - ~3\n105\t    - - RASP\n106\t      - 29%\n107\t      - 61.5%\n108\t      - ~10\n109\t    - - Standard\n110\t      - 27%\n111\t      - 59.3%\n112\t      - ~60\n113\t  figures_description:\n114\t  - 'Collapse dynamics 4-line plot: GRASPrune(step3) < RASP(step10) < Standard(step60)\n115\t    < Unpruned(never). 严重度梯度完整。'\n116\t  analysis: GRASPrune的gradient-based选择策略去除了最多functional redundancy，验证了collapse速度∝redundancy\n117\t    removal程度。四点梯度使诊断工具framing更convincing。\n118\t- name: Multi-seed post-prune eval (5 seeds)\n119\t  plan_id: plan_006\n120\t  description: RASP_20 + Standard_20 post-prune evaluation with 5 seeds for robust\n121\t    variance estimation\n122\t  expected_results:\n123\t    rasp_20_mean_accuracy: 0.295\n124\t    rasp_20_std: 0.012\n125\t    standard_20_mean_accuracy: 0.27\n126\t    standard_20_std: 0.015\n127\t    rasp_vs_standard_p_value: 0.03\n128\t    seeds:\n129\t    - 42\n130\t    - 123\n131\t    - 456\n132\t    - 789\n133\t    - 1024\n134\t    n_per_seed: 1319\n135\t  result_rationale: Post-prune eval是deterministic（greedy decoding），seed影响仅来自calibration\n136\t    data sampling。RASP的CKA scoring对calibration data更稳定（因为CKA captures structural而非instance-level信号），故std略低。5-seed下2.5pp\n137\t    gap可达p<0.05。\n138\t  tables:\n139\t  - name: 'Table: Multi-Seed Post-Prune Accuracy'\n140\t    columns:\n141\t    - Method\n142\t    - Mean±Std\n143\t    - 95% CI\n144\t    - Seeds\n145\t    rows:\n146\t    - - RASP_20\n147\t      - 29.5±1.2%\n148\t      - '[27.1, 31.9]'\n149\t      - 5\n150\t    - - Standard_20\n151\t      - 27.0±1.5%\n152\t      - '[24.0, 30.0]'\n153\t      - 5\n154\t  figures_description:\n155\t  - Box plot with 5 seeds per method, showing RASP略高且方差更小\n156\t  analysis: Post-prune gap达到marginal significance (p=0.03)，但核心论点不依赖此——真正差异在recovery和collapse\n157\t    dynamics。Multi-seed确认pruning本身reproducible。\n158\t- name: Scoring ablation (magnitude/gradient/random)\n159\t  plan_id: plan_007\n160\t  description: 'Ablation pruning at 20%: magnitude-only, gradient-only, random. Isolate\n161\t    CKA contribution'\n162\t  expected_results:\n163\t    magnitude_only_postprune: 0.25\n164\t    gradient_only_postprune: 0.28\n165\t    random_postprune: 0.15\n166\t    magnitude_sft_recovery: 0.56\n167\t    gradient_sft_recovery: 0.58\n168\t    random_sft_recovery: 0.42\n169\t    magnitude_grpo_collapse_step: 40\n170\t    gradient_grpo_collapse_step: 45\n171\t    random_grpo_collapse_step: 8\n172\t  result_rationale: Magnitude-only保留大权重但忽略功能冗余，post-prune与Standard(importance-based)接近。Gradient-only与GRASPrune逻辑相似但无budget约束，略好于magnitude。Random是lower\n173\t    bound。CKA的贡献在于：RASP(31%)>gradient(28%)>magnitude(25%)>random(15%)。GRPO collapse速度中，random最快（随机破坏冗余路径），magnitude/gradient因保留high-importance\n174\t    units而较慢，但仍比Standard快（Standard的importance metric隐式保留了部分冗余）。\n175\t  tables:\n176\t  - name: 'Table: Scoring Ablation Results'\n177\t    columns:\n178\t    - Scoring\n179\t    - Post-Prune\n180\t    - Post-SFT\n181\t    - GRPO Collapse\n182\t    rows:\n183\t    - - RASP (I×(1-F)^α)\n184\t      - 29%\n185\t      - 61.5%\n186\t      - step ~10\n187\t    - - Standard (importance)\n188\t      - 27%\n189\t      - 59.3%\n190\t      - step ~60\n191\t    - - Gradient-only\n192\t      - 28%\n193\t      - 58%\n194\t      - step ~45\n195\t    - - Magnitude-only\n196\t      - 25%\n197\t      - 56%\n198\t      - step ~40\n199\t    - - Random\n200\t      - 15%\n201\t      - 42%\n202\t      - step ~8\n203\t  figures_description:\n204\t  - 'Scatter plot: post-prune accuracy vs GRPO collapse step for all methods, showing\n205\t    RASP is Pareto-dominated point — high SFT but fast collapse'\n206\t  analysis: CKA贡献体现在SFT recovery（+5pp over magnitude），但对GRPO有害（collapse比magnitude/gradient快4-6×）。验证redundancy\n207\t    removal与collapse速度的因果关系。\n208\t- name: Per-structure CKA-recoverability correlation\n209\t  plan_id: plan_008\n210\t  description: Per-head F(h) correlated with activation change post-recovery. Mixed-effects\n211\t    regression\n212\t  expected_results:\n213\t    fh_recovery_correlation_sft: -0.42\n214\t    fh_recovery_correlation_sft_p: 0.001\n215\t    fh_collapse_speed_correlation: 0.55\n216\t    fh_collapse_speed_p: 0.0003\n217\t    mixed_effects_r2: 0.38\n218\t    layer_random_effect_variance: 0.15\n219\t    controlling_for_weight_norm: true\n220\t    controlling_for_gradient_importance: true\n221\t    n_structures: 784\n222\t  result_rationale: F(h)（CKA功能冗余度）高的结构在SFT后activation变化小（r=-0.42）——因为它们的功能已由其他结构承接，不需要恢复。但高F(h)结构的移除与GRPO\n223\t    collapse速度正相关（r=0.55）——因为它们提供的backup paths是RL exploration的安全网。Mixed-effects R²=0.38说明F(h)解释了显著但非全部方差（其他因素如layer\n224\t    position也重要）。\n225\t  tables:\n226\t  - name: 'Table: CKA-Recoverability Regression'\n227\t    columns:\n228\t    - Predictor\n229\t    - β\n230\t    - SE\n231\t    - p-value\n232\t    rows:\n233\t    - - F(h) (CKA redundancy)\n234\t      - -0.42\n235\t      - 0.08\n236\t      - <0.001\n237\t    - - Weight norm\n238\t      - 0.12\n239\t      - 0.05\n240\t      - 0.02\n241\t    - - Gradient importance\n242\t      - 0.08\n243\t      - 0.06\n244\t      - 0.18\n245\t    - - Layer (random)\n246\t      - σ²=0.15\n247\t      - '-'\n248\t      - '-'\n249\t  figures_description:\n250\t  - 'Scatter with regression line: F(h) vs activation change magnitude (left panel,\n251\t    SFT context), F(h) vs time-to-collapse contribution (right panel, GRPO context)'\n252\t  analysis: 机制验证：高冗余结构SFT可安全移除（功能可redistribution），但GRPO需要它们作为exploration buffer。这是Redundancy-Stability\n253\t    Tradeoff的结构层面证据。\n254\t- name: SFT-only recovery comparison\n255\t  plan_id: plan_009\n256\t  description: Same pruned models, SFT only (no GRPO stage). Tests whether pruning\n257\t    strategy优劣在SFT-only pipeline中成立\n258\t  expected_results:\n259\t    rasp_20_sft_only_accuracy: 0.6149\n260\t    standard_20_sft_only_accuracy: 0.5929\n261\t    gap_pp: 2.2\n262\t    p_value: 0.25\n263\t    rasp_25_sft_only_accuracy: 0.57\n264\t    standard_25_sft_only_accuracy: 0.5125\n265\t    gap_25_pp: 5.75\n266\t    p_25_value: 0.008\n267\t  result_rationale: 20%稀疏度下SFT gap仅2.2pp（已有数据，p=0.25不显著）。25%稀疏度放大效应：Standard在更高稀疏度下丢失更多关键结构，SFT难以完全恢复；RASP的CKA-aware选择在25%时保留了更关键的functional\n268\t    units，使recovery gap扩大至5.75pp（p=0.008）。这验证了'SFT下RASP优越性随稀疏度单调递增'。\n269\t  tables:\n270\t  - name: 'Table: SFT-Only Recovery by Sparsity'\n271\t    columns:\n272\t    - Sparsity\n273\t    - RASP SFT\n274\t    - Standard SFT\n275\t    - Gap\n276\t    - p-value\n277\t    rows:\n278\t    - - 20%\n279\t      - 61.49%\n280\t      - 59.29%\n281\t      - +2.2pp\n282\t      - 0.25\n283\t    - - 25%\n284\t      - 57.0%\n285\t      - 51.25%\n286\t      - +5.75pp\n287\t      - 0.008\n288\t  figures_description:\n289\t  - 'Line plot: accuracy vs sparsity for RASP and Standard, diverging as sparsity\n290\t    increases. Error bars show CI narrowing at N=1319.'\n291\t  analysis: SFT gap在25%处achieve significance。Claim 3直接支持：SFT-only pipeline下RASP显著优于Standard，但GRPO\n292\t    pipeline下RASP有害——pruning策略的最优性conditioned on recovery method。\n293\t- name: 25% sparsity full pipeline (RASP + Standard)\n294\t  plan_id: plan_010\n295\t  description: '25% structured pruning: prune → eval → SFT → GRPO for both methods.\n296\t    Core scope expansion.'\n297\t  expected_results:\n298\t    rasp_25_postprune: 0.21\n299\t    standard_25_postprune: 0.16\n300\t    rasp_25_sft_accuracy: 0.57\n301\t    standard_25_sft_accuracy: 0.5125\n302\t    sft_gap_pp: 5.75\n303\t    sft_gap_p_value: 0.008\n304\t    grpo_rasp_25_collapse_step: 4\n305\t    grpo_rasp_25_peak_reward: 0.025\n306\t    grpo_rasp_25_final_frac_zero_std: 0.97\n307\t    grpo_standard_25_collapse_step: 20\n308\t    grpo_standard_25_peak_reward: 0.055\n309\t    grpo_standard_25_step60_frac_zero_std: 0.85\n310\t    collapse_ratio_standard_vs_rasp: 5.0\n311\t  result_rationale: 25%稀疏度下两个关键放大效应：(1) SFT gap从2.2pp扩大至5.75pp，因为Standard在更高稀疏度下不得不移除更多functionally\n312\t    important structures（importance ranking的long tail quality下降），而RASP的CKA-aware selection依然能识别truly\n313\t    redundant structures。(2) GRPO collapse加速：RASP从step10→step4（冗余路径更少，RL exploration更快失去safety\n314\t    net），Standard从step60→step20（相同逻辑但程度较轻）。Collapse ratio从6x(20%)收缩至5x(25%)因为Standard也开始受损严重。\n315\t  tables:\n316\t  - name: 'Table: 25% Sparsity Pipeline Results'\n317\t    columns:\n318\t    - Method\n319\t    - Post-Prune\n320\t    - Post-SFT\n321\t    - GRPO Collapse\n322\t    - GRPO Δ vs SFT\n323\t    rows:\n324\t    - - RASP_25\n325\t      - 21%\n326\t      - 57.0%\n327\t      - step 4\n328\t      - -1.5pp\n329\t    - - Standard_25\n330\t      - 16%\n331\t      - 51.25%\n332\t      - step 20\n333\t      - -2.0pp\n334\t  - name: 'Table: Collapse Dynamics Comparison (20% vs 25%)'\n335\t    columns:\n336\t    - Method\n337\t    - Collapse@20%\n338\t    - Collapse@25%\n339\t    - Acceleration\n340\t    rows:\n341\t    - - RASP\n342\t      - step 10\n343\t      - step 4\n344\t      - 2.5×\n345\t    - - Standard\n346\t      - step 60\n347\t      - step 20\n348\t      - 3×\n349\t  figures_description:\n350\t  - 'Dual-panel: (Left) SFT accuracy vs sparsity showing divergence at 25%. (Right)\n351\t    frac_zero_std curves at 25% showing RASP collapse at step 4 vs Standard at step\n352\t    20.'\n353\t  analysis: 25%是paper的sweet spot：SFT gap达到显著，GRPO collapse更极端，所有效应放大。这使三条claim全部有strong\n354\t    statistical backing。\n355\t- name: 30% sparsity probe (prune + eval only)\n356\t  plan_id: plan_011\n357\t  description: 30% prune + post-prune eval for RASP and Standard. Map threshold where\n358\t    both collapse.\n359\t  expected_results:\n360\t    rasp_30_postprune: 0.1\n361\t    standard_30_postprune: 0.06\n362\t    rasp_30_eos_rate: 0.3\n363\t    standard_30_eos_rate: 0.15\n364\t    both_below_threshold: true\n365\t  result_rationale: '30%已完成pruning（registry: prune_rasp_30 actual=28.7%, prune_standard_30\n366\t    actual=28.5%）。Post-prune eval预期：两者均严重受损但RASP略好。30%接近D005中35% total collapse的阈值，EOS\n367\t    rate极低表明模型结构被严重破坏。RASP 10% > Standard 6%因为CKA-aware selection即使在极端稀疏度下仍能identify最核心的非冗余结构。'\n368\t  tables:\n369\t  - name: 'Table: Sparsity Threshold Mapping'\n370\t    columns:\n371\t    - Sparsity\n372\t    - RASP Post-Prune\n373\t    - Standard Post-Prune\n374\t    - EOS Rate\n375\t    rows:\n376\t    - - 20%\n377\t      - 29%\n378\t      - 27%\n379\t      - '>90%'\n380\t    - - 25%\n381\t      - 21%\n382\t      - 16%\n383\t      - 56-70%\n384\t    - - 30%\n385\t      - 10%\n386\t      - 6%\n387\t      - 15-30%\n388\t  figures_description:\n389\t  - 'Line plot: accuracy degradation curve across sparsity levels. Both methods approach\n390\t    zero around 30-35%. The gap widens then narrows as both collapse.'\n391\t  analysis: 30%标定了'structural death zone'。两者均不可SFT恢复至实用水平（预期<35%），确认paper focus on\n392\t    20-25%的合理性。提供sparsity-accuracy曲线的第三个数据点。\n393\t- name: Extended evaluation (MMLU, HumanEval, MATH-500)\n394\t  plan_id: plan_012\n395\t  description: Best recovered config on OOD benchmarks to show generalization beyond\n396\t    GSM8K\n397\t  expected_results:\n398\t    rasp_20_sft_mmlu: 0.52\n399\t    rasp_20_sft_humaneval: 0.35\n400\t    rasp_20_sft_math500: 0.28\n401\t    standard_20_sft_mmlu: 0.5\n402\t    standard_20_sft_humaneval: 0.33\n403\t    standard_20_sft_math500: 0.26\n404\t    unpruned_sft_mmlu: 0.63\n405\t    unpruned_sft_humaneval: 0.55\n406\t    unpruned_sft_math500: 0.52\n407\t  result_rationale: OOD eval确认SFT recovery不是GSM8K memorization。RASP在所有benchmarks上marginal\n408\t    advantage（1-2pp）与GSM8K pattern一致。MMLU保留较多因为knowledge存储在unpruned layers。HumanEval和MATH-500降幅更大因为需要更多compositional\n409\t    reasoning chains（被pruning破坏）。Unpruned→Pruned的gap在MATH-500最大因为multi-step reasoning最依赖structural\n410\t    integrity。\n411\t  tables:\n412\t  - name: 'Table: Multi-Benchmark Evaluation'\n413\t    columns:\n414\t    - Config\n415\t    - GSM8K\n416\t    - MATH-500\n417\t    - HumanEval\n418\t    - MMLU\n419\t    rows:\n420\t    - - Unpruned\n421\t      - 81.3%\n422\t      - 52%\n423\t      - 55%\n424\t      - 63%\n425\t    - - RASP_20 SFT\n426\t      - 61.5%\n427\t      - 28%\n428\t      - 35%\n429\t      - 52%\n430\t    - - Standard_20 SFT\n431\t      - 59.3%\n432\t      - 26%\n433\t      - 33%\n434\t      - 50%\n435\t  figures_description:\n436\t  - 'Radar chart: 4 benchmarks × 3 configs, showing proportional degradation pattern\n437\t    is consistent'\n438\t  analysis: OOD generalization确认recovery是genuine reasoning restoration而非pattern memorization。RASP\n439\t    advantage跨benchmark一致但不dramatic，支持'marginal SFT advantage'的honest framing。\n440\t- name: Bonsai baseline 20%\n441\t  plan_id: plan_013\n442\t  description: Gradient-free structured pruning (ICML 2025) at 20%. Full pipeline\n443\t    comparison.\n444\t  expected_results:\n445\t    bonsai_20_postprune: 0.22\n446\t    bonsai_20_sft_accuracy: 0.53\n447\t    bonsai_20_grpo_collapse_step: 35\n448\t    bonsai_20_grpo_peak_reward: 0.048\n449\t  result_rationale: Bonsai uses activation-based structural importance (no gradients)，比magnitude-only好但比gradient-based差。Post-prune\n450\t    22%介于random(15%)和Standard(27%)之间。SFT recovery 53%低于Standard因为activation-based\n451\t    scoring在reasoning model上不如gradient-based。GRPO collapse在step 35——比RASP(10)慢但比Standard(60)快，因为Bonsai的importance\n452\t    metric不像Standard那样隐式保留冗余路径。\n453\t  tables:\n454\t  - name: 'Table: All Baselines Comparison'\n455\t    columns:\n456\t    - Method\n457\t    - Type\n458\t    - Post-Prune\n459\t    - Post-SFT\n460\t    - Collapse\n461\t    rows:\n462\t    - - RASP\n463\t      - CKA-aware\n464\t      - 29%\n465\t      - 61.5%\n466\t      - step 10\n467\t    - - Standard\n468\t      - Importance\n469\t      - 27%\n470\t      - 59.3%\n471\t      - step 60\n472\t    - - GRASPrune\n473\t      - Gradient budget\n474\t      - 7%\n475\t      - 41%\n476\t      - step 3\n477\t    - - Bonsai\n478\t      - Activation\n479\t      - 22%\n480\t      - 53%\n481\t      - step 35\n482\t    - - Random\n483\t      - None\n484\t      - 15%\n485\t      - 42%\n486\t      - step 8\n487\t  figures_description:\n488\t  - 'Scatter: SFT recovery (x) vs GRPO collapse step (y) for all 5 methods. Shows\n489\t    inverse relationship for methods that remove more redundancy.'\n490\t  analysis: 5-method comparison构建完整的方法landscape。关键洞见：collapse step与SFT accuracy不是简单正相关——RASP有最高SFT但最快collapse，验证Redundancy-Stability\n491\t    Tradeoff不是artifact of binary comparison。\n492\t- name: CKA reliability analysis\n493\t  plan_id: plan_014\n494\t  description: Split-half consistency and calibration size sensitivity for CKA scoring\n495\t  expected_results:\n496\t    split_half_spearman_rho: 0.94\n497\t    split_half_p_value: 0.0001\n498\t    cal_256_vs_512_rank_correlation: 0.91\n499\t    cal_512_vs_1024_rank_correlation: 0.96\n500\t    cal_256_accuracy: 0.28\n501\t    cal_512_accuracy: 0.31\n502\t    cal_1024_accuracy: 0.31\n503\t    optimal_cal_size: 512\n504\t  result_rationale: CKA measures structural similarity which is a stable property\n505\t    of the network（不像gradient那样sample-dependent）。Split-half ρ=0.94表明CKA scoring高度reproducible。256→512有accuracy提升因为更好估计layer-wise\n506\t    statistics，但512→1024饱和因为CKA kernel已收敛。这证明RASP不需要大量calibration data，512 samples足够。\n507\t  tables:\n508\t  - name: 'Table: CKA Stability Analysis'\n509\t    columns:\n510\t    - Cal Size\n511\t    - Accuracy\n512\t    - Rank Corr vs 512\n513\t    rows:\n514\t    - - 256\n515\t      - 28%\n516\t      - 0.91\n517\t    - - 512\n518\t      - 31%\n519\t      - 1.0\n520\t    - - 1024\n521\t      - 31%\n522\t      - 0.96\n523\t  figures_description:\n524\t  - 'Left: split-half rank correlation histogram (bootstrapped). Right: accuracy vs\n525\t    calibration size curve showing saturation at 512.'\n526\t  analysis: 'CKA scoring is stable and efficient。reviewer concern about calibration\n527\t    sensitivity addressed: 512 samples sufficient, split-half ρ>0.9。'\n528\t- name: α sensitivity ablation (post-SFT)\n529\t  plan_id: plan_015\n530\t  description: Sweep α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2} with full SFT recovery. Paper's single\n531\t    free parameter.\n532\t  expected_results:\n533\t    alpha_0_sft_accuracy: 0.5929\n534\t    alpha_0.25_sft_accuracy: 0.58\n535\t    alpha_0.5_sft_accuracy: 0.59\n536\t    alpha_1.0_sft_accuracy: 0.6149\n537\t    alpha_2.0_sft_accuracy: 0.62\n538\t    alpha_4.0_sft_accuracy: 0.62\n539\t    optimal_alpha: 1.0\n540\t    u_shape_confirmed: true\n541\t    grpo_collapse_alpha_0: 55\n542\t    grpo_collapse_alpha_1: 10\n543\t    grpo_collapse_alpha_2: 7\n544\t  result_rationale: α=0时S(h)=I(h)（Standard），α→∞时S(h)∝(1-F(h))^α（纯CKA，忽略importance）。已有post-prune\n545\t    data showing U-shape：α∈{0,0.25,0.5}≈22-27%，α≥1.0达31-36%。Post-SFT pattern：α=0等同Standard\n546\t    (59.3%)，α=1.0是RASP (61.5%)最优平衡，α=2.0略提升post-prune(36%)但SFT recovery与α=1相当（redundancy过度惩罚导致剪掉一些SFT需要的结构）。GRPO\n547\t    collapse速度：α越大→越多redundancy被移除→collapse越快。α=0(Standard)≈step55（接近v8的60），α=1(RASP)=step10（v9数据），α=2约step7。\n548\t  tables:\n549\t  - name: 'Table: α Sensitivity (20% sparsity, N=1319)'\n550\t    columns:\n551\t    - α\n552\t    - Post-Prune\n553\t    - Post-SFT\n554\t    - GRPO Collapse\n555\t    rows:\n556\t    - - 0.0\n557\t      - 27%\n558\t      - 59.3%\n559\t      - step ~55\n560\t    - - 0.25\n561\t      - 23%\n562\t      - 58%\n563\t      - step ~50\n564\t    - - 0.5\n565\t      - 22%\n566\t      - 59%\n567\t      - step ~45\n568\t    - - 1.0\n569\t      - 31%\n570\t      - 61.5%\n571\t      - step ~10\n572\t    - - 2.0\n573\t      - 36%\n574\t      - 62%\n575\t      - step ~7\n576\t  figures_description:\n577\t  - 'Three-panel: (A) Post-prune accuracy vs α (U-shape). (B) Post-SFT accuracy vs\n578\t    α (monotonic increase from α=0.5). (C) GRPO collapse step vs α (monotonic decrease).\n579\t    Shows SFT and GRPO optimization directions are opposed.'\n580\t  analysis: α controls redundancy-importance tradeoff。Panel C是核心：α越大SFT越好但GRPO越不稳定——这就是Redundancy-Stability\n581\t    Tradeoff在连续parameter space中的表达。α是tuning knob，不是hyperparameter gamble。\n582\t- name: Inference speedup benchmark\n583\t  plan_id: plan_016\n584\t  description: Wall-clock latency and throughput for dense vs 20% RASP vs 20% Standard\n585\t  expected_results:\n586\t    dense_latency_ms: 45\n587\t    rasp_20_latency_ms: 37\n588\t    standard_20_latency_ms: 37\n589\t    speedup_ratio: 1.22\n590\t    dense_throughput_tps: 85\n591\t    rasp_20_throughput_tps: 104\n592\t    standard_20_throughput_tps: 104\n593\t    memory_reduction_pct: 19\n594\t    batch_size: 1\n595\t    seq_len: 512\n596\t  result_rationale: 20%结构化剪枝移除~19%参数（实际sparsity 19%，见registry）。结构化剪枝直接减少矩阵维度，无需专用sparse\n597\t    kernel。理论加速1/(1-0.19)=1.23×，实际~1.22×因为attention和layer norm不被pruned。RASP和Standard\n598\t    speedup相同因为它们移除相同数量的参数（只是选择不同structures）。Memory reduction与parameter reduction线性对应。\n599\t  tables:\n600\t  - name: 'Table: Inference Efficiency'\n601\t    columns:\n602\t    - Model\n603\t    - Params (B)\n604\t    - Latency (ms)\n605\t    - Throughput (tok/s)\n606\t    - Memory (GB)\n607\t    rows:\n608\t    - - Dense\n609\t      - 7.62B\n610\t      - 45\n611\t      - 85\n612\t      - 15.2\n613\t    - - RASP_20\n614\t      - 6.17B\n615\t      - 37\n616\t      - 104\n617\t      - 12.3\n618\t    - - Standard_20\n619\t      - 6.17B\n620\t      - 37\n621\t      - 104\n622\t      - 12.3\n623\t  figures_description:\n624\t  - Bar chart comparing latency/throughput across configs. Both pruned methods identical,\n625\t    ~22% faster than dense.\n626\t  analysis: Structured pruning delivers real wallclock speedup without custom kernels。Efficiency是pruning的practical\n627\t    motivation，但不是paper核心contribution——放在appendix或supplementary。\n628\t- name: Unstructured pruning baseline 20%\n629\t  plan_id: plan_017\n630\t  description: Magnitude-based unstructured pruning at 20% for Self-Healing comparison\n631\t    calibration\n632\t  expected_results:\n633\t    unstructured_20_postprune: 0.55\n634\t    unstructured_20_sft_accuracy: 0.72\n635\t    unstructured_20_grpo_collapse_step: null\n636\t    unstructured_20_grpo_reward_final: 0.35\n637\t    unstructured_20_grpo_no_collapse: true\n638\t    unstructured_vs_structured_gap: 25\n639\t  result_rationale: Unstructured pruning at 20% damage远小于structured（保留所有neuron/head，仅零化individual\n640\t    weights）。Post-prune 55%（vs structured 27-29%）因为network topology完整。SFT recovery至72%因为functional\n641\t    capacity largely preserved。GRPO不collapse因为exploration paths完整——这正是structured pruning\n642\t    unique failure的对照。Self-Healing claims RLVR works at 25% unstructured → 我们的数据应与其一致：unstructured\n643\t    pruning不触发collapse。这calibrates paper的claim为'structured pruning specific'。\n644\t  tables:\n645\t  - name: 'Table: Structured vs Unstructured at 20%'\n646\t    columns:\n647\t    - Pruning Type\n648\t    - Post-Prune\n649\t    - Post-SFT\n650\t    - GRPO Status\n651\t    rows:\n652\t    - - Structured (RASP)\n653\t      - 29%\n654\t      - 61.5%\n655\t      - Collapse step 10\n656\t    - - Structured (Standard)\n657\t      - 27%\n658\t      - 59.3%\n659\t      - Collapse step 60\n660\t    - - Unstructured (Magnitude)\n661\t      - 55%\n662\t      - 72%\n663\t      - No collapse\n664\t    - - Dense (Unpruned)\n665\t      - 81.3%\n666\t      - 81.3%\n667\t      - No collapse\n668\t  figures_description:\n669\t  - 'Collapse dynamics plot: unstructured pruning curve overlaps with unpruned (both\n670\t    stable), while structured methods show distinct collapse patterns'\n671\t  analysis: 'Key differentiation vs Self-Healing: GRPO failure是structural pruning特有的。Unstructured\n672\t    pruning保留all pathway topology，RL exploration不受限。Paper claim narrowed to ''structured\n673\t    pruning causes GRPO collapse''——更精确，更defensible。'\n674\t- name: SFT OOD eval contingency\n675\t  plan_id: plan_018\n676\t  description: Standard_20 SFT model (59.3% GSM8K) evaluated on MATH-500 and HumanEval\n677\t  expected_results:\n678\t    standard_20_sft_math500: 0.26\n679\t    standard_20_sft_humaneval: 0.33\n680\t    rasp_20_sft_math500: 0.28\n681\t    rasp_20_sft_humaneval: 0.35\n682\t    unpruned_sft_math500: 0.52\n683\t    ratio_gsm8k_to_math500_standard: 2.28\n684\t    memorization_ruled_out: true\n685\t  result_rationale: Standard SFT 1%→59.3%(GSM8K)的jump在OOD benchmarks上应按比例衰减但不崩溃。MATH-500比GSM8K难~2×，所以59.3%\n686\t    GSM8K → ~26% MATH-500合理。如果是纯memorization则MATH-500应≈random(~5%)。26%远高于random，确认genuine\n687\t    reasoning recovery。RASP在OOD上保持2pp advantage与GSM8K pattern一致。\n688\t  tables:\n689\t  - name: 'Table: OOD Generalization Check'\n690\t    columns:\n691\t    - Config\n692\t    - GSM8K\n693\t    - MATH-500\n694\t    - HumanEval\n695\t    rows:\n696\t    - - Standard_20 SFT\n697\t      - 59.3%\n698\t      - 26%\n699\t      - 33%\n700\t    - - RASP_20 SFT\n701\t      - 61.5%\n702\t      - 28%\n703\t      - 35%\n704\t  figures_description:\n705\t  - Grouped bars showing consistent RASP advantage across benchmarks, ruling out GSM8K-specific\n706\t    overfitting\n707\t  analysis: Contingency experiment结果positive：OOD performance confirms SFT recovery\n708\t    is genuine。Standard的1%→59.3%不是memorization artifact。Best tier下此experiment是supplementary\n709\t    evidence而非必需。\n710\t- name: Qwen-Math-7B GRPO collapse replication (20%)\n711\t  plan_id: plan_010_cross_model_20\n712\t  description: GRPO on Qwen-Math-7B pruned models to replicate collapse severity gradient\n713\t    on second model\n714\t  expected_results:\n715\t    qwen_rasp_20_sft_accuracy: 0.725\n716\t    qwen_standard_20_sft_accuracy: 0.71\n717\t    qwen_rasp_20_grpo_collapse_step: 8\n718\t    qwen_standard_20_grpo_collapse_step: 45\n719\t    qwen_collapse_ratio: 5.6\n720\t    qwen_rasp_grpo_peak_reward: 0.03\n721\t    qwen_standard_grpo_peak_reward: 0.055\n722\t    cross_model_pattern_replicated: true\n723\t  result_rationale: Qwen-Math-7B SFT accuracy已知(RASP 72.5%, Standard 71%)。GRPO collapse应replicate\n724\t    severity gradient：RASP更快collapse因为CKA-aware selection移除了更多冗余路径。但Qwen-Math的baseline更强（math-specific\n725\t    pretraining），所以collapse略慢于DeepSeek-R1模型（step8 vs step10 for RASP）但比例关系保持。Collapse\n726\t    ratio 5.6×(45/8)与DeepSeek的6×(60/10)相当，验证跨模型一致性。\n727\t  tables:\n728\t  - name: 'Table: Cross-Model Collapse Comparison'\n729\t    columns:\n730\t    - Model\n731\t    - RASP Collapse\n732\t    - Standard Collapse\n733\t    - Ratio\n734\t    rows:\n735\t    - - DeepSeek-R1-7B\n736\t      - step 10\n737\t      - step 60\n738\t      - 6×\n739\t    - - Qwen-Math-7B\n740\t      - step 8\n741\t      - step 45\n742\t      - 5.6×\n743\t  figures_description:\n744\t  - Side-by-side collapse dynamics (frac_zero_std) for both models, showing parallel\n745\t    patterns with similar ratios\n746\t  analysis: 跨模型复现是best tier的核心要求。Ratio在5-6×范围内一致证明Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff是general\n747\t    principle而非model-specific artifact。\n748\t- name: Qwen-Math-7B 25% sparsity GRPO collapse\n749\t  plan_id: plan_010_cross_model_25\n750\t  description: GRPO on Qwen-Math-7B at 25% sparsity. Tests collapse acceleration on\n751\t    second model.\n752\t  expected_results:\n753\t    qwen_rasp_25_sft_accuracy: 0.64\n754\t    qwen_standard_25_sft_accuracy: 0.63\n755\t    qwen_rasp_25_grpo_collapse_step: 3\n756\t    qwen_standard_25_grpo_collapse_step: 18\n757\t    qwen_25_collapse_ratio: 6.0\n758\t    sft_gap_qwen_25_pp: 1.0\n759\t    cross_model_collapse_acceleration: true\n760\t  result_rationale: Qwen-Math 25% SFT已知(RASP 64%, Standard 63%, gap仅1pp)。GRPO collapse进一步加速：RASP\n761\t    step3(vs 20%的step8)，Standard step18(vs 20%的step45)。Acceleration factor ~2.5×与DeepSeek\n762\t    pattern(step4 vs step10)一致。注意Qwen-Math上SFT gap不显著(1pp)但collapse gradient依然清晰——这强化了'RASP对GRPO有害'的claim不依赖于SFT优势的大小。\n763\t  tables:\n764\t  - name: 'Table: Qwen-Math Sparsity × Method × Recovery'\n765\t    columns:\n766\t    - Sparsity\n767\t    - Method\n768\t    - SFT\n769\t    - GRPO Collapse\n770\t    rows:\n771\t    - - 20%\n772\t      - RASP\n773\t      - 72.5%\n774\t      - step 8\n775\t    - - 20%\n776\t      - Standard\n777\t      - 71%\n778\t      - step 45\n779\t    - - 25%\n780\t      - RASP\n781\t      - 64%\n782\t      - step 3\n783\t    - - 25%\n784\t      - Standard\n785\t      - 63%\n786\t      - step 18\n787\t  figures_description:\n788\t  - '2×2 grid of collapse curves: rows=sparsity(20/25), cols=model(DeepSeek/Qwen).\n789\t    All four panels show same RASP<Standard pattern.'\n790\t  analysis: 四个condition(2 models × 2 sparsities)全部replicate collapse severity gradient。这是paper最强的generalization\n791\t    evidence。即使SFT gap在Qwen上不显著，GRPO collapse diagnostic依然robust——strengthens Claim\n792\t    2 (collapse as diagnostic tool)。\n793\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4bc2a3bd-d50f-4f56-b18b-27b29ed56804","uuid":"6be2e0ba-c681-4ebc-bb84-f13baee9c7d2","timestamp":"2026-05-16T15:28:54.001Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T144805/best/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 25%稀疏度放大SFT gap至显著水平，GRPO collapse在两个模型上均加速，三条claim完整成立。RASP既是SFT最优方法又是RLVR\n  collapse诊断工具，Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff跨模型跨稀疏度一致。投EMNLP Main无需降档。\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Full GSM8K eval baseline + pruned models\n  plan_id: plan_001\n  description: N=1319 full eval for unpruned baseline, RASP_20 post-prune, Standard_20\n    post-prune\n  expected_results:\n    unpruned_baseline_accuracy: 0.8127\n    rasp_20_postprune_accuracy: 0.29\n    standard_20_postprune_accuracy: 0.27\n    rasp_vs_standard_gap_pp: 2.0\n    n_total: 1319\n  result_rationale: 已有N=100数据确认RASP 31% vs Standard 27%。N=1319仅收窄CI（±2.4pp），点估计不变。Post-prune\n    gap ~2pp不显著，因为pruning damage尚未通过SFT recovery放大差异。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Post-Prune Accuracy (20% structured, N=1319)'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Accuracy\n    - 95% CI\n    rows:\n    - - Unpruned\n      - 81.27%\n      - ±2.1pp\n    - - RASP_20\n      - 29.0%\n      - ±2.4pp\n    - - Standard_20\n      - 27.0%\n      - ±2.4pp\n  figures_description:\n  - Bar chart showing massive accuracy drop from pruning (81→29/27%) with overlapping\n    CIs between RASP and Standard\n  analysis: Post-prune差异不显著证实pruning damage本身不区分方法，真正差异在recovery阶段才显现。\n- name: Full GSM8K eval all recovered models\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: N=1319 eval for RASP_20 SFT, Standard_20 SFT, RASP_20 GRPO, Standard_20\n    GRPO, unpruned GRPO\n  expected_results:\n    rasp_20_sft_accuracy: 0.6149\n    standard_20_sft_accuracy: 0.5929\n    rasp_20_grpo_step5_accuracy: 0.6065\n    standard_20_grpo_step50_accuracy: 0.5891\n    unpruned_grpo_step100_accuracy: 0.8127\n    sft_gap_rasp_vs_standard_pp: 2.2\n    grpo_delta_rasp_pp: -0.84\n    grpo_delta_standard_pp: -0.38\n    grpo_delta_unpruned_pp: 0.0\n  result_rationale: 已有完整数据。GRPO对所有模型accuracy无正增益（unpruned完全相同1072/1319），pruned模型略降。paper\n    Table 1核心数据已齐全。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 1: Recovery Accuracy (GSM8K, N=1319, greedy)'\n    columns:\n    - Config\n    - SFT\n    - GRPO\n    - Δ(GRPO-SFT)\n    rows:\n    - - Unpruned\n      - 81.27%\n      - 81.27%\n      - +0.00pp\n    - - Standard_20\n      - 59.29%\n      - 58.91%\n      - -0.38pp\n    - - RASP_20\n      - 61.49%\n      - 60.65%\n      - -0.84pp\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Grouped bar chart: SFT vs GRPO accuracy for 3 configs, showing GRPO never improves\n    accuracy'\n  analysis: GRPO reward-accuracy decoupling是universal的；pruning-specific failure是training\n    collapse而非accuracy degradation。\n- name: GRASPrune baseline 20% full pipeline\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: 'GRASPrune at 20% sparsity: prune → eval → SFT → GRPO. ACL 2026 SOTA\n    external baseline'\n  expected_results:\n    postprune_accuracy: 0.07\n    postprune_eos_rate: 0.02\n    post_sft_accuracy: 0.41\n    post_sft_stderr: 0.027\n    post_sft_n1319_accuracy: 0.4\n    grpo_collapse_step: 3\n    grpo_peak_reward: 0.012\n    grpo_final_frac_zero_std: 0.98\n  result_rationale: GRASP post-prune仅7%（已验证），SFT恢复至41%（已验证，p=0.001 vs Standard 64%）。GRASP激进剪枝破坏更多结构冗余，GRPO应在≤5步collapse——比RASP更快。GRASP\n    removes high-gradient structures regardless of functional redundancy，resulting\n    in maximal RLVR instability。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: GRASPrune vs RASP vs Standard Pipeline'\n    columns:\n    - Method\n    - Post-Prune\n    - Post-SFT\n    - GRPO Collapse Step\n    rows:\n    - - GRASPrune\n      - 7%\n      - 41%\n      - ~3\n    - - RASP\n      - 29%\n      - 61.5%\n      - ~10\n    - - Standard\n      - 27%\n      - 59.3%\n      - ~60\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Collapse dynamics 4-line plot: GRASPrune(step3) < RASP(step10) < Standard(step60)\n    < Unpruned(never). 严重度梯度完整。'\n  analysis: GRASPrune的gradient-based选择策略去除了最多functional redundancy，验证了collapse速度∝redundancy\n    removal程度。四点梯度使诊断工具framing更convincing。\n- name: Multi-seed post-prune eval (5 seeds)\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: RASP_20 + Standard_20 post-prune evaluation with 5 seeds for robust\n    variance estimation\n  expected_results:\n    rasp_20_mean_accuracy: 0.295\n    rasp_20_std: 0.012\n    standard_20_mean_accuracy: 0.27\n    standard_20_std: 0.015\n    rasp_vs_standard_p_value: 0.03\n    seeds:\n    - 42\n    - 123\n    - 456\n    - 789\n    - 1024\n    n_per_seed: 1319\n  result_rationale: Post-prune eval是deterministic（greedy decoding），seed影响仅来自calibration\n    data sampling。RASP的CKA scoring对calibration data更稳定（因为CKA captures structural而非instance-level信号），故std略低。5-seed下2.5pp\n    gap可达p<0.05。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Multi-Seed Post-Prune Accuracy'\n    columns:\n    - Method\n    - Mean±Std\n    - 95% CI\n    - Seeds\n    rows:\n    - - RASP_20\n      - 29.5±1.2%\n      - '[27.1, 31.9]'\n      - 5\n    - - Standard_20\n      - 27.0±1.5%\n      - '[24.0, 30.0]'\n      - 5\n  figures_description:\n  - Box plot with 5 seeds per method, showing RASP略高且方差更小\n  analysis: Post-prune gap达到marginal significance (p=0.03)，但核心论点不依赖此——真正差异在recovery和collapse\n    dynamics。Multi-seed确认pruning本身reproducible。\n- name: Scoring ablation (magnitude/gradient/random)\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: 'Ablation pruning at 20%: magnitude-only, gradient-only, random. Isolate\n    CKA contribution'\n  expected_results:\n    magnitude_only_postprune: 0.25\n    gradient_only_postprune: 0.28\n    random_postprune: 0.15\n    magnitude_sft_recovery: 0.56\n    gradient_sft_recovery: 0.58\n    random_sft_recovery: 0.42\n    magnitude_grpo_collapse_step: 40\n    gradient_grpo_collapse_step: 45\n    random_grpo_collapse_step: 8\n  result_rationale: Magnitude-only保留大权重但忽略功能冗余，post-prune与Standard(importance-based)接近。Gradient-only与GRASPrune逻辑相似但无budget约束，略好于magnitude。Random是lower\n    bound。CKA的贡献在于：RASP(31%)>gradient(28%)>magnitude(25%)>random(15%)。GRPO collapse速度中，random最快（随机破坏冗余路径），magnitude/gradient因保留high-importance\n    units而较慢，但仍比Standard快（Standard的importance metric隐式保留了部分冗余）。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Scoring Ablation Results'\n    columns:\n    - Scoring\n    - Post-Prune\n    - Post-SFT\n    - GRPO Collapse\n    rows:\n    - - RASP (I×(1-F)^α)\n      - 29%\n      - 61.5%\n      - step ~10\n    - - Standard (importance)\n      - 27%\n      - 59.3%\n      - step ~60\n    - - Gradient-only\n      - 28%\n      - 58%\n      - step ~45\n    - - Magnitude-only\n      - 25%\n      - 56%\n      - step ~40\n    - - Random\n      - 15%\n      - 42%\n      - step ~8\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter plot: post-prune accuracy vs GRPO collapse step for all methods, showing\n    RASP is Pareto-dominated point — high SFT but fast collapse'\n  analysis: CKA贡献体现在SFT recovery（+5pp over magnitude），但对GRPO有害（collapse比magnitude/gradient快4-6×）。验证redundancy\n    removal与collapse速度的因果关系。\n- name: Per-structure CKA-recoverability correlation\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: Per-head F(h) correlated with activation change post-recovery. Mixed-effects\n    regression\n  expected_results:\n    fh_recovery_correlation_sft: -0.42\n    fh_recovery_correlation_sft_p: 0.001\n    fh_collapse_speed_correlation: 0.55\n    fh_collapse_speed_p: 0.0003\n    mixed_effects_r2: 0.38\n    layer_random_effect_variance: 0.15\n    controlling_for_weight_norm: true\n    controlling_for_gradient_importance: true\n    n_structures: 784\n  result_rationale: F(h)（CKA功能冗余度）高的结构在SFT后activation变化小（r=-0.42）——因为它们的功能已由其他结构承接，不需要恢复。但高F(h)结构的移除与GRPO\n    collapse速度正相关（r=0.55）——因为它们提供的backup paths是RL exploration的安全网。Mixed-effects R²=0.38说明F(h)解释了显著但非全部方差（其他因素如layer\n    position也重要）。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: CKA-Recoverability Regression'\n    columns:\n    - Predictor\n    - β\n    - SE\n    - p-value\n    rows:\n    - - F(h) (CKA redundancy)\n      - -0.42\n      - 0.08\n      - <0.001\n    - - Weight norm\n      - 0.12\n      - 0.05\n      - 0.02\n    - - Gradient importance\n      - 0.08\n      - 0.06\n      - 0.18\n    - - Layer (random)\n      - σ²=0.15\n      - '-'\n      - '-'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter with regression line: F(h) vs activation change magnitude (left panel,\n    SFT context), F(h) vs time-to-collapse contribution (right panel, GRPO context)'\n  analysis: 机制验证：高冗余结构SFT可安全移除（功能可redistribution），但GRPO需要它们作为exploration buffer。这是Redundancy-Stability\n    Tradeoff的结构层面证据。\n- name: SFT-only recovery comparison\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: Same pruned models, SFT only (no GRPO stage). Tests whether pruning\n    strategy优劣在SFT-only pipeline中成立\n  expected_results:\n    rasp_20_sft_only_accuracy: 0.6149\n    standard_20_sft_only_accuracy: 0.5929\n    gap_pp: 2.2\n    p_value: 0.25\n    rasp_25_sft_only_accuracy: 0.57\n    standard_25_sft_only_accuracy: 0.5125\n    gap_25_pp: 5.75\n    p_25_value: 0.008\n  result_rationale: 20%稀疏度下SFT gap仅2.2pp（已有数据，p=0.25不显著）。25%稀疏度放大效应：Standard在更高稀疏度下丢失更多关键结构，SFT难以完全恢复；RASP的CKA-aware选择在25%时保留了更关键的functional\n    units，使recovery gap扩大至5.75pp（p=0.008）。这验证了'SFT下RASP优越性随稀疏度单调递增'。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: SFT-Only Recovery by Sparsity'\n    columns:\n    - Sparsity\n    - RASP SFT\n    - Standard SFT\n    - Gap\n    - p-value\n    rows:\n    - - 20%\n      - 61.49%\n      - 59.29%\n      - +2.2pp\n      - 0.25\n    - - 25%\n      - 57.0%\n      - 51.25%\n      - +5.75pp\n      - 0.008\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Line plot: accuracy vs sparsity for RASP and Standard, diverging as sparsity\n    increases. Error bars show CI narrowing at N=1319.'\n  analysis: SFT gap在25%处achieve significance。Claim 3直接支持：SFT-only pipeline下RASP显著优于Standard，但GRPO\n    pipeline下RASP有害——pruning策略的最优性conditioned on recovery method。\n- name: 25% sparsity full pipeline (RASP + Standard)\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: '25% structured pruning: prune → eval → SFT → GRPO for both methods.\n    Core scope expansion.'\n  expected_results:\n    rasp_25_postprune: 0.21\n    standard_25_postprune: 0.16\n    rasp_25_sft_accuracy: 0.57\n    standard_25_sft_accuracy: 0.5125\n    sft_gap_pp: 5.75\n    sft_gap_p_value: 0.008\n    grpo_rasp_25_collapse_step: 4\n    grpo_rasp_25_peak_reward: 0.025\n    grpo_rasp_25_final_frac_zero_std: 0.97\n    grpo_standard_25_collapse_step: 20\n    grpo_standard_25_peak_reward: 0.055\n    grpo_standard_25_step60_frac_zero_std: 0.85\n    collapse_ratio_standard_vs_rasp: 5.0\n  result_rationale: 25%稀疏度下两个关键放大效应：(1) SFT gap从2.2pp扩大至5.75pp，因为Standard在更高稀疏度下不得不移除更多functionally\n    important structures（importance ranking的long tail quality下降），而RASP的CKA-aware selection依然能识别truly\n    redundant structures。(2) GRPO collapse加速：RASP从step10→step4（冗余路径更少，RL exploration更快失去safety\n    net），Standard从step60→step20（相同逻辑但程度较轻）。Collapse ratio从6x(20%)收缩至5x(25%)因为Standard也开始受损严重。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: 25% Sparsity Pipeline Results'\n    columns:\n    - Method\n    - Post-Prune\n    - Post-SFT\n    - GRPO Collapse\n    - GRPO Δ vs SFT\n    rows:\n    - - RASP_25\n      - 21%\n      - 57.0%\n      - step 4\n      - -1.5pp\n    - - Standard_25\n      - 16%\n      - 51.25%\n      - step 20\n      - -2.0pp\n  - name: 'Table: Collapse Dynamics Comparison (20% vs 25%)'\n    columns:\n    - Method\n    - Collapse@20%\n    - Collapse@25%\n    - Acceleration\n    rows:\n    - - RASP\n      - step 10\n      - step 4\n      - 2.5×\n    - - Standard\n      - step 60\n      - step 20\n      - 3×\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Dual-panel: (Left) SFT accuracy vs sparsity showing divergence at 25%. (Right)\n    frac_zero_std curves at 25% showing RASP collapse at step 4 vs Standard at step\n    20.'\n  analysis: 25%是paper的sweet spot：SFT gap达到显著，GRPO collapse更极端，所有效应放大。这使三条claim全部有strong\n    statistical backing。\n- name: 30% sparsity probe (prune + eval only)\n  plan_id: plan_011\n  description: 30% prune + post-prune eval for RASP and Standard. Map threshold where\n    both collapse.\n  expected_results:\n    rasp_30_postprune: 0.1\n    standard_30_postprune: 0.06\n    rasp_30_eos_rate: 0.3\n    standard_30_eos_rate: 0.15\n    both_below_threshold: true\n  result_rationale: '30%已完成pruning（registry: prune_rasp_30 actual=28.7%, prune_standard_30\n    actual=28.5%）。Post-prune eval预期：两者均严重受损但RASP略好。30%接近D005中35% total collapse的阈值，EOS\n    rate极低表明模型结构被严重破坏。RASP 10% > Standard 6%因为CKA-aware selection即使在极端稀疏度下仍能identify最核心的非冗余结构。'\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Sparsity Threshold Mapping'\n    columns:\n    - Sparsity\n    - RASP Post-Prune\n    - Standard Post-Prune\n    - EOS Rate\n    rows:\n    - - 20%\n      - 29%\n      - 27%\n      - '>90%'\n    - - 25%\n      - 21%\n      - 16%\n      - 56-70%\n    - - 30%\n      - 10%\n      - 6%\n      - 15-30%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Line plot: accuracy degradation curve across sparsity levels. Both methods approach\n    zero around 30-35%. The gap widens then narrows as both collapse.'\n  analysis: 30%标定了'structural death zone'。两者均不可SFT恢复至实用水平（预期<35%），确认paper focus on\n    20-25%的合理性。提供sparsity-accuracy曲线的第三个数据点。\n- name: Extended evaluation (MMLU, HumanEval, MATH-500)\n  plan_id: plan_012\n  description: Best recovered config on OOD benchmarks to show generalization beyond\n    GSM8K\n  expected_results:\n    rasp_20_sft_mmlu: 0.52\n    rasp_20_sft_humaneval: 0.35\n    rasp_20_sft_math500: 0.28\n    standard_20_sft_mmlu: 0.5\n    standard_20_sft_humaneval: 0.33\n    standard_20_sft_math500: 0.26\n    unpruned_sft_mmlu: 0.63\n    unpruned_sft_humaneval: 0.55\n    unpruned_sft_math500: 0.52\n  result_rationale: OOD eval确认SFT recovery不是GSM8K memorization。RASP在所有benchmarks上marginal\n    advantage（1-2pp）与GSM8K pattern一致。MMLU保留较多因为knowledge存储在unpruned layers。HumanEval和MATH-500降幅更大因为需要更多compositional\n    reasoning chains（被pruning破坏）。Unpruned→Pruned的gap在MATH-500最大因为multi-step reasoning最依赖structural\n    integrity。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Multi-Benchmark Evaluation'\n    columns:\n    - Config\n    - GSM8K\n    - MATH-500\n    - HumanEval\n    - MMLU\n    rows:\n    - - Unpruned\n      - 81.3%\n      - 52%\n      - 55%\n      - 63%\n    - - RASP_20 SFT\n      - 61.5%\n      - 28%\n      - 35%\n      - 52%\n    - - Standard_20 SFT\n      - 59.3%\n      - 26%\n      - 33%\n      - 50%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Radar chart: 4 benchmarks × 3 configs, showing proportional degradation pattern\n    is consistent'\n  analysis: OOD generalization确认recovery是genuine reasoning restoration而非pattern memorization。RASP\n    advantage跨benchmark一致但不dramatic，支持'marginal SFT advantage'的honest framing。\n- name: Bonsai baseline 20%\n  plan_id: plan_013\n  description: Gradient-free structured pruning (ICML 2025) at 20%. Full pipeline\n    comparison.\n  expected_results:\n    bonsai_20_postprune: 0.22\n    bonsai_20_sft_accuracy: 0.53\n    bonsai_20_grpo_collapse_step: 35\n    bonsai_20_grpo_peak_reward: 0.048\n  result_rationale: Bonsai uses activation-based structural importance (no gradients)，比magnitude-only好但比gradient-based差。Post-prune\n    22%介于random(15%)和Standard(27%)之间。SFT recovery 53%低于Standard因为activation-based\n    scoring在reasoning model上不如gradient-based。GRPO collapse在step 35——比RASP(10)慢但比Standard(60)快，因为Bonsai的importance\n    metric不像Standard那样隐式保留冗余路径。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: All Baselines Comparison'\n    columns:\n    - Method\n    - Type\n    - Post-Prune\n    - Post-SFT\n    - Collapse\n    rows:\n    - - RASP\n      - CKA-aware\n      - 29%\n      - 61.5%\n      - step 10\n    - - Standard\n      - Importance\n      - 27%\n      - 59.3%\n      - step 60\n    - - GRASPrune\n      - Gradient budget\n      - 7%\n      - 41%\n      - step 3\n    - - Bonsai\n      - Activation\n      - 22%\n      - 53%\n      - step 35\n    - - Random\n      - None\n      - 15%\n      - 42%\n      - step 8\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter: SFT recovery (x) vs GRPO collapse step (y) for all 5 methods. Shows\n    inverse relationship for methods that remove more redundancy.'\n  analysis: 5-method comparison构建完整的方法landscape。关键洞见：collapse step与SFT accuracy不是简单正相关——RASP有最高SFT但最快collapse，验证Redundancy-Stability\n    Tradeoff不是artifact of binary comparison。\n- name: CKA reliability analysis\n  plan_id: plan_014\n  description: Split-half consistency and calibration size sensitivity for CKA scoring\n  expected_results:\n    split_half_spearman_rho: 0.94\n    split_half_p_value: 0.0001\n    cal_256_vs_512_rank_correlation: 0.91\n    cal_512_vs_1024_rank_correlation: 0.96\n    cal_256_accuracy: 0.28\n    cal_512_accuracy: 0.31\n    cal_1024_accuracy: 0.31\n    optimal_cal_size: 512\n  result_rationale: CKA measures structural similarity which is a stable property\n    of the network（不像gradient那样sample-dependent）。Split-half ρ=0.94表明CKA scoring高度reproducible。256→512有accuracy提升因为更好估计layer-wise\n    statistics，但512→1024饱和因为CKA kernel已收敛。这证明RASP不需要大量calibration data，512 samples足够。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: CKA Stability Analysis'\n    columns:\n    - Cal Size\n    - Accuracy\n    - Rank Corr vs 512\n    rows:\n    - - 256\n      - 28%\n      - 0.91\n    - - 512\n      - 31%\n      - 1.0\n    - - 1024\n      - 31%\n      - 0.96\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Left: split-half rank correlation histogram (bootstrapped). Right: accuracy vs\n    calibration size curve showing saturation at 512.'\n  analysis: 'CKA scoring is stable and efficient。reviewer concern about calibration\n    sensitivity addressed: 512 samples sufficient, split-half ρ>0.9。'\n- name: α sensitivity ablation (post-SFT)\n  plan_id: plan_015\n  description: Sweep α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2} with full SFT recovery. Paper's single\n    free parameter.\n  expected_results:\n    alpha_0_sft_accuracy: 0.5929\n    alpha_0.25_sft_accuracy: 0.58\n    alpha_0.5_sft_accuracy: 0.59\n    alpha_1.0_sft_accuracy: 0.6149\n    alpha_2.0_sft_accuracy: 0.62\n    alpha_4.0_sft_accuracy: 0.62\n    optimal_alpha: 1.0\n    u_shape_confirmed: true\n    grpo_collapse_alpha_0: 55\n    grpo_collapse_alpha_1: 10\n    grpo_collapse_alpha_2: 7\n  result_rationale: α=0时S(h)=I(h)（Standard），α→∞时S(h)∝(1-F(h))^α（纯CKA，忽略importance）。已有post-prune\n    data showing U-shape：α∈{0,0.25,0.5}≈22-27%，α≥1.0达31-36%。Post-SFT pattern：α=0等同Standard\n    (59.3%)，α=1.0是RASP (61.5%)最优平衡，α=2.0略提升post-prune(36%)但SFT recovery与α=1相当（redundancy过度惩罚导致剪掉一些SFT需要的结构）。GRPO\n    collapse速度：α越大→越多redundancy被移除→collapse越快。α=0(Standard)≈step55（接近v8的60），α=1(RASP)=step10（v9数据），α=2约step7。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: α Sensitivity (20% sparsity, N=1319)'\n    columns:\n    - α\n    - Post-Prune\n    - Post-SFT\n    - GRPO Collapse\n    rows:\n    - - 0.0\n      - 27%\n      - 59.3%\n      - step ~55\n    - - 0.25\n      - 23%\n      - 58%\n      - step ~50\n    - - 0.5\n      - 22%\n      - 59%\n      - step ~45\n    - - 1.0\n      - 31%\n      - 61.5%\n      - step ~10\n    - - 2.0\n      - 36%\n      - 62%\n      - step ~7\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Three-panel: (A) Post-prune accuracy vs α (U-shape). (B) Post-SFT accuracy vs\n    α (monotonic increase from α=0.5). (C) GRPO collapse step vs α (monotonic decrease).\n    Shows SFT and GRPO optimization directions are opposed.'\n  analysis: α controls redundancy-importance tradeoff。Panel C是核心：α越大SFT越好但GRPO越不稳定——这就是Redundancy-Stability\n    Tradeoff在连续parameter space中的表达。α是tuning knob，不是hyperparameter gamble。\n- name: Inference speedup benchmark\n  plan_id: plan_016\n  description: Wall-clock latency and throughput for dense vs 20% RASP vs 20% Standard\n  expected_results:\n    dense_latency_ms: 45\n    rasp_20_latency_ms: 37\n    standard_20_latency_ms: 37\n    speedup_ratio: 1.22\n    dense_throughput_tps: 85\n    rasp_20_throughput_tps: 104\n    standard_20_throughput_tps: 104\n    memory_reduction_pct: 19\n    batch_size: 1\n    seq_len: 512\n  result_rationale: 20%结构化剪枝移除~19%参数（实际sparsity 19%，见registry）。结构化剪枝直接减少矩阵维度，无需专用sparse\n    kernel。理论加速1/(1-0.19)=1.23×，实际~1.22×因为attention和layer norm不被pruned。RASP和Standard\n    speedup相同因为它们移除相同数量的参数（只是选择不同structures）。Memory reduction与parameter reduction线性对应。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Inference Efficiency'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Params (B)\n    - Latency (ms)\n    - Throughput (tok/s)\n    - Memory (GB)\n    rows:\n    - - Dense\n      - 7.62B\n      - 45\n      - 85\n      - 15.2\n    - - RASP_20\n      - 6.17B\n      - 37\n      - 104\n      - 12.3\n    - - Standard_20\n      - 6.17B\n      - 37\n      - 104\n      - 12.3\n  figures_description:\n  - Bar chart comparing latency/throughput across configs. Both pruned methods identical,\n    ~22% faster than dense.\n  analysis: Structured pruning delivers real wallclock speedup without custom kernels。Efficiency是pruning的practical\n    motivation，但不是paper核心contribution——放在appendix或supplementary。\n- name: Unstructured pruning baseline 20%\n  plan_id: plan_017\n  description: Magnitude-based unstructured pruning at 20% for Self-Healing comparison\n    calibration\n  expected_results:\n    unstructured_20_postprune: 0.55\n    unstructured_20_sft_accuracy: 0.72\n    unstructured_20_grpo_collapse_step: null\n    unstructured_20_grpo_reward_final: 0.35\n    unstructured_20_grpo_no_collapse: true\n    unstructured_vs_structured_gap: 25\n  result_rationale: Unstructured pruning at 20% damage远小于structured（保留所有neuron/head，仅零化individual\n    weights）。Post-prune 55%（vs structured 27-29%）因为network topology完整。SFT recovery至72%因为functional\n    capacity largely preserved。GRPO不collapse因为exploration paths完整——这正是structured pruning\n    unique failure的对照。Self-Healing claims RLVR works at 25% unstructured → 我们的数据应与其一致：unstructured\n    pruning不触发collapse。这calibrates paper的claim为'structured pruning specific'。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Structured vs Unstructured at 20%'\n    columns:\n    - Pruning Type\n    - Post-Prune\n    - Post-SFT\n    - GRPO Status\n    rows:\n    - - Structured (RASP)\n      - 29%\n      - 61.5%\n      - Collapse step 10\n    - - Structured (Standard)\n      - 27%\n      - 59.3%\n      - Collapse step 60\n    - - Unstructured (Magnitude)\n      - 55%\n      - 72%\n      - No collapse\n    - - Dense (Unpruned)\n      - 81.3%\n      - 81.3%\n      - No collapse\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Collapse dynamics plot: unstructured pruning curve overlaps with unpruned (both\n    stable), while structured methods show distinct collapse patterns'\n  analysis: 'Key differentiation vs Self-Healing: GRPO failure是structural pruning特有的。Unstructured\n    pruning保留all pathway topology，RL exploration不受限。Paper claim narrowed to ''structured\n    pruning causes GRPO collapse''——更精确，更defensible。'\n- name: SFT OOD eval contingency\n  plan_id: plan_018\n  description: Standard_20 SFT model (59.3% GSM8K) evaluated on MATH-500 and HumanEval\n  expected_results:\n    standard_20_sft_math500: 0.26\n    standard_20_sft_humaneval: 0.33\n    rasp_20_sft_math500: 0.28\n    rasp_20_sft_humaneval: 0.35\n    unpruned_sft_math500: 0.52\n    ratio_gsm8k_to_math500_standard: 2.28\n    memorization_ruled_out: true\n  result_rationale: Standard SFT 1%→59.3%(GSM8K)的jump在OOD benchmarks上应按比例衰减但不崩溃。MATH-500比GSM8K难~2×，所以59.3%\n    GSM8K → ~26% MATH-500合理。如果是纯memorization则MATH-500应≈random(~5%)。26%远高于random，确认genuine\n    reasoning recovery。RASP在OOD上保持2pp advantage与GSM8K pattern一致。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: OOD Generalization Check'\n    columns:\n    - Config\n    - GSM8K\n    - MATH-500\n    - HumanEval\n    rows:\n    - - Standard_20 SFT\n      - 59.3%\n      - 26%\n      - 33%\n    - - RASP_20 SFT\n      - 61.5%\n      - 28%\n      - 35%\n  figures_description:\n  - Grouped bars showing consistent RASP advantage across benchmarks, ruling out GSM8K-specific\n    overfitting\n  analysis: Contingency experiment结果positive：OOD performance confirms SFT recovery\n    is genuine。Standard的1%→59.3%不是memorization artifact。Best tier下此experiment是supplementary\n    evidence而非必需。\n- name: Qwen-Math-7B GRPO collapse replication (20%)\n  plan_id: plan_010_cross_model_20\n  description: GRPO on Qwen-Math-7B pruned models to replicate collapse severity gradient\n    on second model\n  expected_results:\n    qwen_rasp_20_sft_accuracy: 0.725\n    qwen_standard_20_sft_accuracy: 0.71\n    qwen_rasp_20_grpo_collapse_step: 8\n    qwen_standard_20_grpo_collapse_step: 45\n    qwen_collapse_ratio: 5.6\n    qwen_rasp_grpo_peak_reward: 0.03\n    qwen_standard_grpo_peak_reward: 0.055\n    cross_model_pattern_replicated: true\n  result_rationale: Qwen-Math-7B SFT accuracy已知(RASP 72.5%, Standard 71%)。GRPO collapse应replicate\n    severity gradient：RASP更快collapse因为CKA-aware selection移除了更多冗余路径。但Qwen-Math的baseline更强（math-specific\n    pretraining），所以collapse略慢于DeepSeek-R1模型（step8 vs step10 for RASP）但比例关系保持。Collapse\n    ratio 5.6×(45/8)与DeepSeek的6×(60/10)相当，验证跨模型一致性。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Cross-Model Collapse Comparison'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - RASP Collapse\n    - Standard Collapse\n    - Ratio\n    rows:\n    - - DeepSeek-R1-7B\n      - step 10\n      - step 60\n      - 6×\n    - - Qwen-Math-7B\n      - step 8\n      - step 45\n      - 5.6×\n  figures_description:\n  - Side-by-side collapse dynamics (frac_zero_std) for both models, showing parallel\n    patterns with similar ratios\n  analysis: 跨模型复现是best tier的核心要求。Ratio在5-6×范围内一致证明Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff是general\n    principle而非model-specific artifact。\n- name: Qwen-Math-7B 25% sparsity GRPO collapse\n  plan_id: plan_010_cross_model_25\n  description: GRPO on Qwen-Math-7B at 25% sparsity. Tests collapse acceleration on\n    second model.\n  expected_results:\n    qwen_rasp_25_sft_accuracy: 0.64\n    qwen_standard_25_sft_accuracy: 0.63\n    qwen_rasp_25_grpo_collapse_step: 3\n    qwen_standard_25_grpo_collapse_step: 18\n    qwen_25_collapse_ratio: 6.0\n    sft_gap_qwen_25_pp: 1.0\n    cross_model_collapse_acceleration: true\n  result_rationale: Qwen-Math 25% SFT已知(RASP 64%, Standard 63%, gap仅1pp)。GRPO collapse进一步加速：RASP\n    step3(vs 20%的step8)，Standard step18(vs 20%的step45)。Acceleration factor ~2.5×与DeepSeek\n    pattern(step4 vs step10)一致。注意Qwen-Math上SFT gap不显著(1pp)但collapse gradient依然清晰——这强化了'RASP对GRPO有害'的claim不依赖于SFT优势的大小。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Qwen-Math Sparsity × Method × Recovery'\n    columns:\n    - Sparsity\n    - Method\n    - SFT\n    - GRPO Collapse\n    rows:\n    - - 20%\n      - RASP\n      - 72.5%\n      - step 8\n    - - 20%\n      - Standard\n      - 71%\n      - step 45\n    - - 25%\n      - RASP\n      - 64%\n      - step 3\n    - - 25%\n      - Standard\n      - 63%\n      - step 18\n  figures_description:\n  - '2×2 grid of collapse curves: rows=sparsity(20/25), cols=model(DeepSeek/Qwen).\n    All four panels show same RASP<Standard pattern.'\n  analysis: 四个condition(2 models × 2 sparsities)全部replicate collapse severity gradient。这是paper最强的generalization\n    evidence。即使SFT gap在Qwen上不显著，GRPO collapse diagnostic依然robust——strengthens Claim\n    2 (collapse as diagnostic tool)。\n","numLines":793,"startLine":1,"totalLines":793}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011tvLHSr4sDpJLDfVFn9aFk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've now read the full paper and the review context YAML. Let me now dispatch two reviewers in parallel for the full review process.\n\nThe paper is about \"The Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff: Why CKA-Aware Pruning Helps SFT but Breaks RLVR in Reasoning Models\". Let me set up the full dream review with:\n\n- R1: Methods + Experiments\n- R2: Novelty + Related Work\n\nThen I'll do the 4-step roundtable process.\n\nLet me dispatch both reviewers in parallel as agents.\n\nKey information from the paper I need to convey to each reviewer:\n\n\nThe work proposes RASP, a CKA-based pruning method that uses a scoring function combining importance and stability metrics, and reveals a critical finding: structures that are safely redundant for supervised fine-tuning become essential for maintaining exploration stability during reinforcement learning from reasoning. The authors demonstrate that GRPO training on pruned models initially shows reward improvements without accuracy gains, then collapses, and they argue this collapse severity can diagnose structural criticality.\n\nNow I'm checking which of the planned experiments actually made it into the paper by cross-referencing the imagined experiment list against the tables and results presented. The remaining experiments round out the coverage—inference speedup benchmarks, unstructured pruning baselines, and cross-model validation on Qwen-Math all check out against their respective tables. With all 18 planned experiments accounted for, I'm ready to move forward with writing up the methods and novelty sections in parallel.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":36144,"cache_read_input_tokens":22960,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":36144},"output_tokens":18,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4bc2a3bd-d50f-4f56-b18b-27b29ed56804","uuid":"05dd647a-ee69-4ff2-86c9-365334411a93"}
